#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""SYRD-422: the interactive role-plan prompt, against the launcher it came out of.

The seven definitions behind the part of `switchyard new` that asks which roles
to run and on what -- the two implementer-role constants, the implementer field,
the per-role runtime/model/effort prompt, the whole-plan prompt, its pairs-only
wrapper and the owner-account check -- moved unchanged into
`scripts/role_plan_prompt.py`; the launcher re-exports all seven. This pins what
makes that safe:

- **No cycle, one set of objects**, whichever module is imported first; the
  module alone loads nothing of Switchyard's; its only definition-time defaults
  are the `input` and `print` builtins; the two annotation types are imported
  under TYPE_CHECKING only; `pwd` is the shared module.
- **Seams (rule 24):** every name the seven read -- each other, the launcher's
  yes/no prompt, runtime field, role selection type, role validator, CLI
  defaults and owner command prefix, and the prompt schema, model and effort
  fields, runtime catalog and terminal selector it imports -- is read through
  the launcher as often as before, so a patch there reaches it: every case
  below wraps them there, recorded, and rebinds the CLI defaults and both
  moved constants on the launcher to see the effect.
- **Callers:** `new_project_phases.py` reads the plan prompt through the
  launcher; no launcher definition reads any of the seven.
- **The behaviour is the baseline's:** the questions in order, every line shown,
  the choices and defaults, custom roles, models and efforts and their
  validation, filtering, cancelling and every retry cap, the owner's model list
  read as the owner or withheld with the reason said, and every refusal's text.
  `GOLDEN` below was produced by running the BASELINE launcher's own functions
  over the very cases embedded here (`gold422.py`), not typed; it is
  byte-identical whether generated under `env -i` or in a normal role pane.

No provider CLI, account or network is touched: the answers are scripted, the
model-list runner, the owner command prefix and the account lookup stand in,
recorded. Spawns, every exec, signals, account and group lookups and socket
connections are refused for each case.
"""

